WEBVTT

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:13.210
Ooh! Uh, Captain,
do you have a minute?

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.213
Just about a minute.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.373
I'm on my way
to the shuttle bay.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.474
I thought last night
went well, didn't you?

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.677
Extremely well.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:19.878
Everyone had a lot of fun.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.149
I was thinking of making it
a regular feature...

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.450
say, uh, once a month?

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.855
It's certainly worth a try.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:28.156
And, Captain, you were
especially good last night.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.161
Thanks, Neelix.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.162
It's been a while.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.754
You'd never know.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:35.734
Uh, Captain, um,
do you think, I mean,

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:38.670
uh, l-I-I-I was wondering...

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.172
What is it, Neelix?

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.470
Could you possibly
keep Mr. Tuvok busy

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:43.806
on the Bridge that evening?

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.309
I'm sure something
could be arranged.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.974
Our secret, Neelix.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:50.846
We never had this discussion.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.154
Harry's clarinet solo was okay.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.565
I could have done
without Tuvok's reading

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.798
of Vulcan poetry,
but the highlight of the evening

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:15.467
was definitely Kathryn Janeway
portraying "The Dying Swan."

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.635
I learned that dance
when I was six years old.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:20.305
I assure you, it was the hit
of the beginning ballet class.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.335
I don't doubt it.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.871
If Neelix has
another talent night,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.076
I hope you reprise it.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.551
Oh, no. Not until certain
other people take their turn...

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.883
the ship's First
Officer, for instance.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.980
Me? Get up in front of people
and perform?

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.285
I don't think so.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:34.157
Come on, Chakotay, there
must be some talent you have

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.525
that people would enjoy.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.189
Maybe I could stand
with an apple on my head

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.322
and you could phaser it off.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:40.666
Sounds great.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.962
If I miss, I get to be Captain.

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:45.538
Atmospheric turbulence...

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.971
we might be
in for a rough landing.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:47.995
Funny, a minute ago,

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.406
there wasn't any indication
of rough weather.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.105
I'm reading even more
severe storms near the surface.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.306
Ion lightning.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.009
Maybe we better try
the fifth planet instead.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.744
Come back here
when things have cleared up.

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.386
I think we took a lightning hit.

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:03.514
Attitude control is out.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:04.921
I'm switching to manual.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.187
The navigational system's down.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:10.287
Reverse engines!

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.457
Full thrusters!

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:15.059
Warning. Hydrazine gas leak.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:17.092
Altitude, 12 kilometers.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:18.968
Hull temperature, 4,000 degrees.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.438
We have to reduce speed.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.373
I'll try the emergency
antigrav thrusters.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:02.645
Kathryn!

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.480
Kathryn!

00:04:58.263 --> 00:04:59.355
Kathryn!

00:04:59.398 --> 00:05:00.729
Kathryn!

00:05:10.709 --> 00:05:12.506
No!

00:05:12.544 --> 00:05:13.533
Warning.

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:17.242
Hydrazine gas levels
at 112 parts per million.

00:05:17.282 --> 00:05:19.750
Begin evacuation procedures.

00:05:58.023 --> 00:05:59.183
Hang on, Kathryn.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:11.392
Breathe, damn it.
Breathe.

00:06:15.407 --> 00:06:16.669
Don't you die on me now.

00:06:16.708 --> 00:06:18.107
Come on, Kathryn... breathe!

00:06:24.049 --> 00:06:25.277
Listen to me, Kathryn.

00:06:25.317 --> 00:06:27.512
You've got to breathe.

00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:29.714
Breathe! Breathe!

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:32.656
Come on. Come on!

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:38.421
Yes.

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:41.894
Chakotay...

00:06:44.603 --> 00:06:45.570
Oh...

00:06:45.604 --> 00:06:47.435
Don't ever do that to me again.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.933
Thanks.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:53.972
You went into shock.

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:57.743
You gave me quite a scare
there for a minute.

00:06:57.783 --> 00:06:59.751
This should help
reduce your cranial swelling.

00:06:59.785 --> 00:07:02.015
You should have a headache
for awhile.

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:04.316
I'll live with it.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:07.616
We need to set up
a homing signal.

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.824
Hey, take it easy.

00:07:10.862 --> 00:07:12.830
Oh... I'm all right.

00:07:12.864 --> 00:07:15.856
Chakotay, we're going
to need the blankets...

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:17.958
...and the rations.

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:20.772
I can get them.

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:23.536
You set up the homing signal.

00:07:23.575 --> 00:07:24.872
Here.

00:07:27.913 --> 00:07:30.211
At least the storm
seems to be dying.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:31.773
Hmm.

00:07:54.039 --> 00:07:55.529
What were you looking at?

00:07:55.574 --> 00:07:57.542
There are phaser burns
on the hull.

00:07:57.576 --> 00:07:59.066
I don't think it was
lightning strikes that hit us.

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:00.601
I think we were shot down.

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:01.908
By whom?

00:08:01.947 --> 00:08:03.209
I don't know.

00:08:03.248 --> 00:08:04.476
I'm going back to see
if I can get

00:08:04.516 --> 00:08:05.847
an energy signature
from the burns.

00:08:05.884 --> 00:08:07.215
Chakotay, the homing signal...

00:08:07.252 --> 00:08:09.584
we might be telling someone
just where to find us.

00:08:09.621 --> 00:08:12.522
Disconnect it
while I scan the shuttle.

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:16.791
Oh...

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.630
Can you tell anything?

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:30.642
The signatures are Vidiian.

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:31.643
Vidiian?

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.304
I thought we'd moved
beyond their space.

00:08:33.345 --> 00:08:34.903
If they shot us down,
you can be sure

00:08:34.946 --> 00:08:36.140
they'll be coming for us.

00:08:36.181 --> 00:08:37.705
We need to find a hiding place.

00:08:39.751 --> 00:08:40.911
What is it?

00:08:40.952 --> 00:08:42.112
Life-forms.

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:43.280
50 meters from here.

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:44.289
They're coming this way.

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:45.290
Let's go.

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:46.951
There's another group
in this direction.

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:48.617
We're surrounded.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:49.627
Let's take cover.

00:08:49.661 --> 00:08:50.650
We'll have to fight.

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:04.909
Back off now.

00:09:04.943 --> 00:09:06.274
We'll fire if we have to.

00:09:06.311 --> 00:09:07.300
Back off!

00:09:09.681 --> 00:09:11.273
Chakotay!

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:29.265
Harry's clarinet solo was okay.

00:09:29.301 --> 00:09:31.201
I could have done
without Tuvok's reading

00:09:31.236 --> 00:09:33.830
of Vulcan poetry,
but the highlight of the evening

00:09:33.872 --> 00:09:36.807
was definitely Kathryn Janeway
portraying "The Dying Swan."

00:09:36.842 --> 00:09:39.072
I learned that dance
when I was six years old.

00:09:39.111 --> 00:09:40.442
I assure you...

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:41.446
Wait a minute.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:42.708
What's happening here?

00:09:42.748 --> 00:09:44.375
You're right.

00:09:44.416 --> 00:09:46.350
We have been here before.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:50.051
Do you remember Vidiians?

00:09:50.088 --> 00:09:52.682
Yes. They shot us down
and attacked us.

00:09:52.724 --> 00:09:53.691
We may have wandered

00:09:53.725 --> 00:09:55.659
into some kind
of repeating time loop.

00:09:55.694 --> 00:09:57.184
I'm going to scan
for temporal anomalies.

00:09:58.663 --> 00:10:00.597
Whatever's going on,
let's change tactics this time.

00:10:00.632 --> 00:10:01.963
Let's not try to land
on that planet.

00:10:02.067 --> 00:10:02.965
Agreed.

00:10:03.068 --> 00:10:06.128
I don't see any evidence
of temporal flux

00:10:06.171 --> 00:10:07.729
or any kind of anomaly,
for that matter.

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:08.933
Or of Vidiian ships.

00:10:08.974 --> 00:10:10.134
So far, so good.

00:10:10.175 --> 00:10:11.802
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:10:11.843 --> 00:10:13.470
Chakotay to Voyager.
Do you read us?

00:10:13.512 --> 00:10:14.911
We're out of range.

00:10:14.946 --> 00:10:17.312
I'd still like to figure
out what happened to us.

00:10:17.349 --> 00:10:18.543
Send a subspace message

00:10:18.583 --> 00:10:19.982
that we won't be
landing on the planet.

00:10:20.051 --> 00:10:21.075
Tell them that we'll be looking

00:10:21.119 --> 00:10:22.381
for evidence
of temporal anomalies.

00:10:24.589 --> 00:10:26.648
I see a ship approaching
at high impulse.

00:10:26.691 --> 00:10:27.885
It's on an intercept course.

00:10:27.926 --> 00:10:28.893
Is it Vidiian?

00:10:28.927 --> 00:10:29.985
Yes.

00:10:30.061 --> 00:10:31.221
I've got it.

00:10:31.263 --> 00:10:32.992
It's a warship
loaded with weaponry.

00:10:33.064 --> 00:10:33.996
It's closing fast.

00:10:34.065 --> 00:10:34.997
Can we outrun it?

00:10:35.066 --> 00:10:36.294
We can try.

00:10:41.339 --> 00:10:43.807
They're 200,000 kilometers
away and gaining.

00:10:43.842 --> 00:10:45.867
Setting evasive pattern
delta four.

00:10:45.911 --> 00:10:47.378
They're powering weapons.

00:10:47.412 --> 00:10:48.436
Shields up.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.175
Stand by all phaser arrays.

00:10:56.621 --> 00:10:58.521
Shields down to 84 percent.

00:10:58.557 --> 00:10:59.888
Returning fire.

00:11:03.929 --> 00:11:05.726
- Nice aim.
- It didn't stop them.

00:11:06.465 --> 00:11:08.729
We've lost shields.

00:11:08.767 --> 00:11:10.325
Firing starboard array.

00:11:10.368 --> 00:11:13.337
That one
hit the reactant injectors.

00:11:13.371 --> 00:11:15.066
Shut them down.
They'll leak antimatter.

00:11:15.106 --> 00:11:16.368
The magnetic fields are failing.

00:11:16.408 --> 00:11:17.705
The gas-flow separators
are down.

00:11:17.742 --> 00:11:19.573
Dump the core.

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:41.194
It's looking more and more
like we're in a time loop.

00:11:41.233 --> 00:11:43.258
The question is:
How do we break it?

00:11:43.301 --> 00:11:44.632
Let's retrace our steps...

00:11:44.669 --> 00:11:46.432
get back to the part
of space we were in

00:11:46.471 --> 00:11:47.802
before all this
started happening.

00:11:47.839 --> 00:11:49.136
Agreed.

00:11:49.174 --> 00:11:51.335
If we're experiencing
a temporal field,

00:11:51.376 --> 00:11:53.105
a tachyon burst
might disperse it.

00:11:54.145 --> 00:11:55.134
Chakotay.

00:11:56.548 --> 00:11:58.277
Let me guess...
it's a Vidiian ship.

00:11:58.316 --> 00:11:59.283
Two Vidiian ships.

00:11:59.317 --> 00:12:01.148
Still 20 million
kilometers away,

00:12:01.186 --> 00:12:02.380
but headed right for us.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:03.717
Sacajawea to Voyager.

00:12:03.755 --> 00:12:05.222
Do you read us?

00:12:05.257 --> 00:12:07.589
You've just come into com range,
Commander.

00:12:07.626 --> 00:12:09.753
We're being pursued
by two Vidiian ships.

00:12:09.794 --> 00:12:12.354
Set a course for our shuttle
and have weapons powered.

00:12:12.397 --> 00:12:13.728
We also believe
we're experiencing

00:12:13.765 --> 00:12:16.131
some kind of temporal
phenomenon, a time loop.

00:12:16.167 --> 00:12:17.657
Make certain you scan
for anomalies.

00:12:17.702 --> 00:12:19.727
Aye, Captain.
We're on our way.

00:12:19.771 --> 00:12:21.068
If you're going to emit
that tachyon burst,

00:12:21.106 --> 00:12:22.073
you'd better do it now.

00:12:22.107 --> 00:12:23.074
In a couple of minutes,

00:12:23.108 --> 00:12:24.200
those ships'll be
right on top of us.

00:12:24.242 --> 00:12:26.301
Here goes.

00:12:30.348 --> 00:12:32.179
I can't tell if it's
affecting anything.

00:12:32.217 --> 00:12:33.445
The Vidiians are almost
within range.

00:12:33.485 --> 00:12:34.577
Ready weapons.

00:12:42.427 --> 00:12:43.394
What happened?

00:12:43.428 --> 00:12:44.895
They just vanished.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.693
But I'm picking up
a residual temporal signature.

00:12:46.731 --> 00:12:48.995
Then those ships must've been
part of the time loop.

00:12:50.168 --> 00:12:52.469
And the tachyon burst
disrupted it.

00:12:52.602 --> 00:12:53.660
And not a minute too soon.

00:12:53.703 --> 00:12:55.830
I was getting awfully tired
of talking about talent night.

00:12:55.872 --> 00:12:57.840
Voyager to Sacajawea.

00:12:57.874 --> 00:13:01.002
We will rendezvous with you
in approximately four minutes.

00:13:01.044 --> 00:13:04.013
Believe me, Tuvok,
we're looking forward to it.

00:13:14.324 --> 00:13:15.757
Good to have you back, Captain.

00:13:15.792 --> 00:13:16.759
Good to be here.

00:13:16.793 --> 00:13:17.953
I'd still like to get
to the bottom

00:13:18.061 --> 00:13:19.653
of whatever was happening
to us in that shuttle.

00:13:19.696 --> 00:13:22.722
Did Voyager detect any evidence
of a temporal field?

00:13:22.765 --> 00:13:24.562
To my knowledge, we did not.

00:13:24.601 --> 00:13:26.899
Let's run a second level
temporal scan.

00:13:26.936 --> 00:13:29.131
I'd feel better entering
this part of space

00:13:29.172 --> 00:13:31.072
if I knew what caused
the phenomenon.

00:13:31.107 --> 00:13:32.734
Phenomenon? I'm not sure
what you mean, Captain.

00:13:32.775 --> 00:13:35.266
The time loop, or whatever
it was we ran into out there.

00:13:35.311 --> 00:13:36.300
Time loop?

00:13:36.346 --> 00:13:37.472
We told you.

00:13:37.514 --> 00:13:40.972
Chakotay and I experienced
some kind of temporal loop.

00:13:41.017 --> 00:13:42.279
It involved the Vidiians.

00:13:42.318 --> 00:13:43.683
They'd attack and kill us

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:46.245
and then we'd be sitting
in the shuttle again.

00:13:46.289 --> 00:13:48.484
Tell them.

00:13:48.525 --> 00:13:49.492
We were on our way

00:13:49.526 --> 00:13:50.925
to the second planet
of a binary system...

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.222
To collect
some nitrogenase compound,

00:13:52.262 --> 00:13:54.492
but we encountered a storm
and we crashed.

00:13:54.531 --> 00:13:56.795
And then we were attacked
by the Vidiians,

00:13:56.833 --> 00:13:59.233
but we managed to escape
and get back here.

00:13:59.269 --> 00:14:01.567
You and the Commander
were checked by the Doctor

00:14:01.604 --> 00:14:03.094
who treated your injuries

00:14:03.139 --> 00:14:05.505
and you proceeded
here to the Bridge.

00:14:05.542 --> 00:14:07.908
But I don't remember anything
about a repeating time loop.

00:14:09.479 --> 00:14:11.606
You don't remember
how we kept ending up

00:14:11.648 --> 00:14:14.242
back in the shuttle
talking about talent night?

00:14:18.021 --> 00:14:21.184
Then I'm the only one who
recalls things differently.

00:14:21.224 --> 00:14:23.385
Something strange
is going on here.

00:14:23.426 --> 00:14:25.724
I'll have the Doctor examine me.

00:14:26.896 --> 00:14:30.161
In the meantime, I still want
those temporal scans.

00:14:32.035 --> 00:14:34.026
You heard the Captain.
Let's get moving.

00:14:37.407 --> 00:14:40.205
I ran a micro-cellular scan
after you returned to the ship.

00:14:40.243 --> 00:14:42.871
I have just analyzed
the results.

00:14:42.912 --> 00:14:44.311
What did you find?

00:14:44.347 --> 00:14:47.612
You have contracted a disease.

00:14:48.952 --> 00:14:50.647
The Vidiian phage.

00:14:50.687 --> 00:14:52.484
The phage.

00:14:53.489 --> 00:14:54.888
What about Chakotay?

00:14:54.924 --> 00:14:56.323
Is he infected, too?

00:14:56.359 --> 00:14:59.260
No, Commander Chakotay shows
no signs of the disease.

00:14:59.295 --> 00:15:00.762
How did I get it?

00:15:00.797 --> 00:15:03.789
You said one of the Vidiians
grabbed you.

00:15:03.833 --> 00:15:06.267
It may be that the virus
was transferred in that way.

00:15:06.302 --> 00:15:08.395
But we've encountered Vidiians
like that before

00:15:08.438 --> 00:15:10.599
and had physical contact
with them.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.074
No one's ever gotten sick
that way.

00:15:14.477 --> 00:15:17.037
I can't offer an explanation
at this point.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:19.071
It may be that the phage virus
has mutated

00:15:19.115 --> 00:15:20.412
to become more infectious.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:22.315
I believe, however,
this explains

00:15:22.352 --> 00:15:24.946
the hallucinations
you've described.

00:15:25.021 --> 00:15:27.683
There is often concomitant
stress to the thalamus

00:15:27.724 --> 00:15:29.419
in the early stages
of the disease.

00:15:29.459 --> 00:15:32.087
It is known to cause
a kind of dementia

00:15:32.128 --> 00:15:33.925
that produces hallucinations.

00:15:33.963 --> 00:15:35.430
What's the prognosis?

00:15:35.465 --> 00:15:37.524
I wish I could tell you,
Captain.

00:15:37.567 --> 00:15:40.229
For the moment, it would be best
if you remain in Sick Bay

00:15:40.269 --> 00:15:41.566
under quarantine.

00:15:41.604 --> 00:15:42.571
Of course.

00:15:42.605 --> 00:15:44.937
The fact that the virus
has acted so quickly

00:15:44.974 --> 00:15:46.168
raises the possibility

00:15:46.209 --> 00:15:48.370
that others on the
crew may be infected.

00:15:48.411 --> 00:15:50.345
But you studied the phage
in great detail.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:52.507
Have you made any progress
in finding a cure?

00:15:52.548 --> 00:15:54.106
I hadn't pursued the matter

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:56.948
since we seemed to have moved
beyond Vidiian space,

00:15:56.986 --> 00:15:59.955
but I'll now redouble
my efforts.

00:15:59.989 --> 00:16:03.083
In the meantime, I'd like
to give you a sedative.

00:16:05.128 --> 00:16:06.288
Captain?

00:16:09.966 --> 00:16:12.935
I'll be running a series
of deep-level tissue scans.

00:16:13.036 --> 00:16:14.298
I understand.

00:16:14.337 --> 00:16:16.430
There.

00:16:16.472 --> 00:16:18.804
That should give you
a good night's sleep.

00:16:18.841 --> 00:16:20.536
I'll erect a bio-force field

00:16:20.576 --> 00:16:23.511
and I promise you, Captain,
I won't deactivate myself

00:16:23.546 --> 00:16:25.411
until I have some answers
for you.

00:16:25.448 --> 00:16:26.745
Doctor?

00:16:28.184 --> 00:16:30.778
I know I'm in good hands.

00:17:09.592 --> 00:17:10.923
Doctor?

00:17:14.297 --> 00:17:16.857
Ah. You're awake.

00:17:16.899 --> 00:17:17.923
How long have I been asleep?

00:17:17.967 --> 00:17:19.764
Almost 40 hours.

00:17:19.802 --> 00:17:21.099
Forty?

00:17:22.472 --> 00:17:24.099
I'm afraid this strain
of the phage

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.368
is particularly virulent.

00:17:25.408 --> 00:17:27.433
It's spreading rapidly.

00:17:29.345 --> 00:17:31.404
Have you?

00:17:31.447 --> 00:17:34.109
Is there any hope of a cure?

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:37.278
I regret to inform you
that I have been unsuccessful.

00:17:38.855 --> 00:17:40.789
Then what's the next step?

00:17:40.823 --> 00:17:43.291
I've given that a great deal
of thought.

00:17:43.326 --> 00:17:46.193
The prospects
are unpleasant, Captain.

00:17:46.229 --> 00:17:49.164
You face a lingering,
painful death

00:17:49.198 --> 00:17:51.666
marked by increasing periods
of dementia

00:17:51.701 --> 00:17:53.498
and eventual insanity.

00:17:53.536 --> 00:17:54.628
I see.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:55.637
I've come to the conclusion

00:17:55.671 --> 00:17:57.195
that there's only one
humane course of action.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.502
What's that?

00:17:58.541 --> 00:17:59.803
Euthanasia.

00:18:01.377 --> 00:18:02.344
What?

00:18:02.378 --> 00:18:03.743
It would be wrong to subject you

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:05.441
to such a prolonged
and painful death.

00:18:05.481 --> 00:18:07.506
The crew would also
be adversely affected

00:18:07.550 --> 00:18:09.142
if that were to happen.

00:18:09.185 --> 00:18:11.483
Well, surely, there are other
options to explore, Doctor.

00:18:11.521 --> 00:18:14.513
B'Elanna's DNA, for instance.

00:18:14.557 --> 00:18:18.084
It's coded to produce
antibodies against the phage.

00:18:18.127 --> 00:18:20.459
Klingon DNA might provide
a vaccine for the disease,

00:18:20.496 --> 00:18:21.554
but not a cure.

00:18:21.597 --> 00:18:23.929
I'm sorry, Captain.

00:18:23.966 --> 00:18:26.264
The space within the force field
is filling with a neural toxin.

00:18:26.302 --> 00:18:29.135
It is fast-acting and merciful.

00:18:29.172 --> 00:18:30.469
Turn it off.

00:18:30.506 --> 00:18:31.495
That's an order, Doctor!

00:18:31.541 --> 00:18:35.204
Please relax
and take deep breaths.

00:18:35.244 --> 00:18:36.973
It will be over
more quickly that way.

00:18:38.781 --> 00:18:40.840
Computer, delete Emergency
Medical Hologram.

00:18:40.883 --> 00:18:44.375
A security code is required
for that command.

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:46.980
Security code:
Janeway-lambda-three.

00:18:48.024 --> 00:18:50.515
That code is not recognized.

00:18:52.562 --> 00:18:54.189
I'm the Captain.
Delete the EMH.

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:57.757
A security code
is required for that command.

00:18:57.800 --> 00:18:59.131
Don't do this.

00:19:01.637 --> 00:19:03.400
It isn't right.

00:19:19.689 --> 00:19:21.156
Chakotay.

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:22.214
I know.

00:19:22.258 --> 00:19:23.225
We're back.

00:19:23.259 --> 00:19:24.556
That's it.

00:19:24.594 --> 00:19:25.925
That must be the anomaly.

00:19:25.995 --> 00:19:27.622
That's what's behind all this.

00:19:27.663 --> 00:19:29.722
It's exerting
a gravitomagnetic force.

00:19:29.765 --> 00:19:32.290
We've got to get away from it.
Divert all power to the engines.

00:19:32.335 --> 00:19:34.303
Changing course.

00:19:34.337 --> 00:19:35.497
We're still being drawn
toward it.

00:19:35.538 --> 00:19:37.438
Reverse engines.
Full power.

00:19:37.473 --> 00:19:38.565
Structural integrity
is weakening.

00:19:38.608 --> 00:19:40.200
Reinforce the hull.

00:19:40.243 --> 00:19:41.301
Captain,

00:19:41.344 --> 00:19:42.106
maybe we should go in.

00:19:42.144 --> 00:19:43.611
- No.
- Listen to me.

00:19:43.646 --> 00:19:45.079
Maybe we're doing this
all wrong.

00:19:45.114 --> 00:19:46.843
Maybe the thing to do
is fly into it.

00:19:46.883 --> 00:19:48.510
No, I don't believe that.
We've got to get away.

00:19:48.551 --> 00:19:49.813
It's going to tear
the shuttle apart.

00:19:49.852 --> 00:19:50.841
The hull is breaching.

00:19:57.894 --> 00:19:58.918
Don't you die on me, Kathryn.

00:19:58.961 --> 00:20:00.690
Chakotay, what's happening?

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:01.754
Start breathing!

00:20:01.797 --> 00:20:04.960
Breathe, damn it.
Breathe!

00:20:05.001 --> 00:20:08.368
Don't do this to me, Kathryn.

00:20:08.404 --> 00:20:09.701
Come on, Kathryn... breathe!

00:20:09.739 --> 00:20:10.933
Can't you hear me?

00:20:10.973 --> 00:20:12.372
Don't you die on me.

00:20:12.408 --> 00:20:14.638
Come on, breathe.

00:20:14.677 --> 00:20:16.668
Kathryn, listen to me.

00:20:16.712 --> 00:20:18.703
You have to breathe.

00:20:18.748 --> 00:20:20.306
Start breathing!

00:20:20.349 --> 00:20:22.874
Come on! Come on!

00:20:29.025 --> 00:20:31.152
No, Kathryn!

00:20:33.062 --> 00:20:34.495
You can't die.

00:20:45.942 --> 00:20:48.376
Chakotay, I'm here.

00:20:48.411 --> 00:20:50.003
Voyager to Sacajawea.

00:20:50.046 --> 00:20:51.013
Do you read us?

00:20:51.113 --> 00:20:52.307
Yes, Voyager.

00:20:52.348 --> 00:20:53.315
How far are you?

00:20:53.349 --> 00:20:54.373
I have an emergency here.

00:20:54.417 --> 00:20:55.885
We're in orbit, Commander.

00:20:56.018 --> 00:20:56.916
We've located you,

00:20:56.952 --> 00:20:58.852
but transporters
won't function in the storm.

00:20:58.888 --> 00:21:01.448
A shuttle is on its way
to the surface now.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.424
The Captain's dead.

00:21:03.459 --> 00:21:05.586
We have to get her back
to Sick Bay.

00:21:05.628 --> 00:21:07.687
The Doctor may still
be able to revive her.

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:09.322
The away team
should be with you in minutes.

00:21:09.365 --> 00:21:10.332
Acknowledged.

00:21:10.366 --> 00:21:12.231
I know you can't see me
or hear me.

00:21:12.268 --> 00:21:13.860
I don't know what's going on.

00:21:13.903 --> 00:21:15.302
But I am here, Chakotay.

00:21:15.337 --> 00:21:16.429
I'm not dead.

00:21:16.472 --> 00:21:19.270
Kathryn,
we're going to get you back.

00:21:20.743 --> 00:21:22.438
Ten milligrams cordrazine.

00:21:22.478 --> 00:21:25.106
We'll use it in conjunction
with the cortical stimulator.

00:21:25.147 --> 00:21:27.479
Now.

00:21:27.516 --> 00:21:28.949
No pulse, no blood pressure.

00:21:28.984 --> 00:21:30.975
Minimum electrical activity
in the mid-brain.

00:21:31.053 --> 00:21:33.988
No measurable response
in the cerebral cortex.

00:21:34.056 --> 00:21:34.784
Again.

00:21:37.059 --> 00:21:39.527
Doctor, we're getting
a thready pulse.

00:21:39.561 --> 00:21:41.688
Quickly. 75 milligrams
inaprovaline.

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:44.927
I'll begin
direct synaptic stimulation.

00:21:52.942 --> 00:21:54.534
Pulse is weakening.

00:21:54.576 --> 00:21:56.009
We're losing her again.

00:21:56.045 --> 00:21:57.273
Cortical stimulator.

00:21:57.313 --> 00:21:58.541
Now.

00:22:01.417 --> 00:22:03.942
No vital signs,
no brain activity.

00:22:03.986 --> 00:22:04.782
Again!

00:22:07.189 --> 00:22:08.156
No change.

00:22:08.190 --> 00:22:09.157
- Again.
- Doctor...

00:22:09.191 --> 00:22:10.556
Don't question me.
Again.

00:22:19.368 --> 00:22:21.427
Make a note in the log.

00:22:21.470 --> 00:22:23.631
Death occurred at 0320 hours.

00:22:23.672 --> 00:22:27.768
Cause... massive
cerebrovascular collapse.

00:22:37.286 --> 00:22:38.913
Computer...

00:22:38.954 --> 00:22:41.252
confirm Janeway voice pattern.

00:22:43.625 --> 00:22:45.593
Kes, you're a telepath.

00:22:45.627 --> 00:22:48.721
You've been able to sense things
others can't.

00:22:48.764 --> 00:22:50.925
Kes, can you sense me?

00:22:50.966 --> 00:22:53.867
Kes...

00:22:53.902 --> 00:22:55.802
please go to the science lab

00:22:55.838 --> 00:22:58.272
and prepare
the autopsy protocols.

00:23:06.782 --> 00:23:07.942
I'm here, Kes.

00:23:08.017 --> 00:23:10.042
I'm staying with you
until you realize it.

00:23:16.225 --> 00:23:17.920
Captain?

00:23:21.597 --> 00:23:23.155
Did you feel that, Kes?

00:23:23.198 --> 00:23:24.187
It was me.

00:23:24.233 --> 00:23:25.757
Kes to Commander Chakotay.

00:23:25.801 --> 00:23:27.234
I need to talk to you
right away.

00:23:28.937 --> 00:23:30.666
Maybe it was nothing,

00:23:30.706 --> 00:23:31.968
but I had the strongest feeling

00:23:32.007 --> 00:23:34.635
that the Captain was there
in the corridor with me.

00:23:34.676 --> 00:23:35.700
It is possible

00:23:35.744 --> 00:23:37.803
that in your distress
over the Captain's death,

00:23:37.846 --> 00:23:39.871
you imagined that you
were aware of her.

00:23:39.915 --> 00:23:42.076
It was more than that,
I'm sure of it.

00:23:42.117 --> 00:23:43.641
In the past, Kes
has shown an ability

00:23:43.685 --> 00:23:44.947
to detect an unseen presence.

00:23:44.987 --> 00:23:46.978
I think we have to take
her seriously.

00:23:47.056 --> 00:23:48.148
The Captain's consciousness

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:50.090
might have phase-shifted
out of our reality.

00:23:50.125 --> 00:23:52.593
She could be in some kind
of alternate dimension

00:23:52.628 --> 00:23:53.925
in subspace.

00:23:53.962 --> 00:23:55.657
We have to find her somehow.

00:23:55.697 --> 00:23:57.995
Harry and I can run
a full subspace sweep.

00:23:58.100 --> 00:23:59.761
See if we can come up
with anything.

00:23:59.802 --> 00:24:01.269
Get on it.
It's your top priority.

00:24:01.303 --> 00:24:02.895
Neelix, help the crew
with this.

00:24:02.938 --> 00:24:05.702
Keep their morale up
until we can get some answers.

00:24:05.741 --> 00:24:07.470
Yes, sir.
Right away.

00:24:07.509 --> 00:24:09.841
Commander, I suggest
I work with Kes.

00:24:09.878 --> 00:24:11.243
I may be able to help her

00:24:11.280 --> 00:24:12.804
increase the range
of her perceptions.

00:24:12.848 --> 00:24:13.815
Good idea.

00:24:13.849 --> 00:24:16.215
Tom, we'll take duty stations.

00:24:19.555 --> 00:24:21.045
That's more like it.

00:24:24.359 --> 00:24:26.554
I've reconfigured
the lateral sensor array

00:24:26.595 --> 00:24:28.290
to scan subspace.

00:24:28.330 --> 00:24:30.560
Don't forget
to run a magneton sweep.

00:24:30.599 --> 00:24:32.123
The forward array
is ready to scan

00:24:32.167 --> 00:24:33.498
for temporal phase shifting...

00:24:33.535 --> 00:24:35.730
chroniton particles
or field flux.

00:24:35.771 --> 00:24:39.104
I'm going to activate
the magneton scanner.

00:24:39.141 --> 00:24:41.109
It might pick up
an anomalous presence.

00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:47.280
Now what?

00:25:02.831 --> 00:25:03.957
Daddy?

00:25:08.837 --> 00:25:09.929
Who are you?

00:25:09.972 --> 00:25:11.769
Are you responsible
for what's going on here?

00:25:11.807 --> 00:25:13.798
You know who I am, Kathryn.

00:25:13.842 --> 00:25:16.402
My father died
over 15 years ago.

00:25:16.445 --> 00:25:19.107
Yes. Drowned under
the polar ice cap

00:25:19.148 --> 00:25:20.740
on Tau Ceti Prime.

00:25:20.782 --> 00:25:22.477
It was devastating to you.

00:25:22.518 --> 00:25:25.078
You may be an hallucination
or some kind of projection

00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:27.452
of my own imagination,
but you are not my father.

00:25:27.489 --> 00:25:30.424
Kathryn, Kathryn.

00:25:30.459 --> 00:25:33.223
I raised you to be
a doubter and a skeptic,

00:25:33.262 --> 00:25:36.561
to look at the world
with a scientist's eye,

00:25:36.598 --> 00:25:39.624
but in this instance,
that won't work.

00:25:39.668 --> 00:25:42.330
Why not? If you know
what's going on here, tell me.

00:25:42.371 --> 00:25:43.963
Isn't it clear?

00:25:44.039 --> 00:25:45.336
You're dead.

00:25:45.374 --> 00:25:47.968
You died in that shuttle crash.

00:25:48.043 --> 00:25:49.067
No, no, no.

00:25:49.111 --> 00:25:50.305
That's not possible.

00:25:50.345 --> 00:25:52.506
I understand your confusion...

00:25:52.548 --> 00:25:54.982
your refusal to accept
what's happened.

00:25:55.017 --> 00:25:57.645
I went through the same thing
after my accident.

00:25:57.686 --> 00:25:58.983
What do you mean?

00:25:59.021 --> 00:26:02.320
I went back to you
and your mother and your sister

00:26:02.357 --> 00:26:04.257
after I died for a long time,

00:26:04.293 --> 00:26:06.693
until I realized it was futile.

00:26:06.728 --> 00:26:10.027
That's what happens
when death is unexpected.

00:26:10.065 --> 00:26:13.296
One's consciousness
isn't prepared to let go.

00:26:13.335 --> 00:26:14.393
"Consciousness"?

00:26:14.436 --> 00:26:15.869
Is that what you're calling me...

00:26:15.904 --> 00:26:17.769
"Kathryn's consciousness"?

00:26:17.806 --> 00:26:19.330
For want of a better word.

00:26:19.374 --> 00:26:21.501
Some say "ghost" or "spirit."

00:26:21.543 --> 00:26:23.738
We all heard the stories
and thought they were

00:26:23.779 --> 00:26:25.804
the product
of vivid imaginations

00:26:25.847 --> 00:26:28.042
or self-induced hysteria.

00:26:28.083 --> 00:26:31.382
I'll admit, I was surprised
when I found they were true.

00:26:31.420 --> 00:26:34.912
If you stayed with me
after you died,

00:26:34.957 --> 00:26:37.585
you should be able
to tell me what happened then.

00:26:37.626 --> 00:26:39.526
You were so grief stricken,

00:26:39.561 --> 00:26:41.756
you fell
into a terrible depression.

00:26:41.797 --> 00:26:44.925
You spent months in bed
sleeping away your days,

00:26:44.967 --> 00:26:47.231
rather than confronting
your feelings.

00:26:47.269 --> 00:26:48.702
I'm not sure
what would have happened

00:26:48.737 --> 00:26:51.638
if your sister hadn't forced you
into the real world again.

00:26:51.673 --> 00:26:53.504
If you are an hallucination,
a part of me,

00:26:53.542 --> 00:26:54.702
you'd know those things.

00:26:54.743 --> 00:26:59.544
Kathryn, remember... several
times after I died, you woke up

00:26:59.581 --> 00:27:00.912
thinking I was
in the room with you.

00:27:00.949 --> 00:27:04.385
You told your sister
it felt absolutely real.

00:27:04.419 --> 00:27:06.717
That's because it was real.

00:27:06.755 --> 00:27:08.279
I was there
trying to convince you

00:27:08.323 --> 00:27:10.223
to get on with your life.

00:27:10.259 --> 00:27:14.025
Just for the sake of argument,
let's say you're right.

00:27:14.062 --> 00:27:15.256
What's next?

00:27:15.297 --> 00:27:16.730
That's up to you.

00:27:16.765 --> 00:27:18.255
Eventually, you will cross over.

00:27:18.300 --> 00:27:19.426
The only question is

00:27:19.468 --> 00:27:21.800
how long it will take you
to give up this world.

00:27:21.837 --> 00:27:23.236
Cross over to where?

00:27:23.272 --> 00:27:26.173
I don't know what to call it.

00:27:26.208 --> 00:27:30.008
Another state
of consciousness...

00:27:31.313 --> 00:27:34.942
unlike anything we ever
could have imagined in life.

00:27:35.050 --> 00:27:38.144
It's not a frightening
place, Kathryn.

00:27:38.186 --> 00:27:42.316
It's full of joy
and indescribable wonder.

00:27:42.357 --> 00:27:43.824
Kes sensed I was here.

00:27:43.859 --> 00:27:45.326
They're looking for me.

00:27:45.360 --> 00:27:48.693
People have felt the presence
of ghosts throughout the ages,

00:27:48.730 --> 00:27:53.394
but the technology to find them
still hasn't been invented.

00:27:53.435 --> 00:27:55.198
They won't give up easily.

00:27:55.237 --> 00:27:57.535
But they will give up
eventually.

00:27:57.572 --> 00:28:01.975
They'll accept what's happened
and that's what you have to do.

00:28:03.512 --> 00:28:05.139
Kes did it once.
She can do it again.

00:28:05.180 --> 00:28:06.545
I'm going to help her.

00:28:06.581 --> 00:28:10.608
If that's what you feel
you need to do, I understand.

00:28:18.160 --> 00:28:20.424
Let us try one more time.

00:28:22.297 --> 00:28:25.926
Open yourself
to the impressions around you,

00:28:25.967 --> 00:28:29.698
the thoughts, the minds
that are on this ship.

00:28:29.738 --> 00:28:33.071
All the minds
that are on this ship.

00:28:33.108 --> 00:28:36.509
I hear them.

00:28:36.545 --> 00:28:38.179
So many voices.

00:28:38.312 --> 00:28:40.143
They are a turbulent storm

00:28:40.181 --> 00:28:44.379
and you are the one who must
rise above the tempest

00:28:44.418 --> 00:28:46.352
to a place that is quiet.

00:28:46.387 --> 00:28:48.252
It's difficult.

00:28:48.289 --> 00:28:51.452
You must lift yourself
from the confusion of the storm.

00:28:51.492 --> 00:28:56.191
Soar into the quiet space
among the stars

00:28:56.230 --> 00:28:58.858
where everything is still.

00:29:00.801 --> 00:29:02.894
Yes, I'm in that place now.

00:29:02.937 --> 00:29:04.905
Is there a voice
that you can hear...

00:29:04.972 --> 00:29:08.567
a single voice isolated
in the stillness?

00:29:09.777 --> 00:29:11.745
Kes, I'm here.

00:29:11.779 --> 00:29:14.247
Focus on me, on my voice.

00:29:14.281 --> 00:29:17.011
There are only two beings

00:29:17.051 --> 00:29:19.679
in the void...
you and Captain Janeway.

00:29:19.720 --> 00:29:22.780
Nothing else exists
that can interfere.

00:29:22.823 --> 00:29:26.156
Can you hear her voice,
however faintly?

00:29:26.193 --> 00:29:28.058
I'm trying.

00:29:28.095 --> 00:29:29.722
Is there anything,

00:29:29.763 --> 00:29:31.890
any presence
in the void with you?

00:29:37.004 --> 00:29:38.699
I don't think so.
I can't hear anything.

00:29:38.739 --> 00:29:40.104
Kes, keep trying.

00:29:40.140 --> 00:29:41.801
You have to find me.

00:29:41.842 --> 00:29:43.275
Now, I am with you,

00:29:43.310 --> 00:29:45.574
moving through the quiet space,

00:29:45.613 --> 00:29:48.912
my thoughts joined with yours,

00:29:48.949 --> 00:29:51.417
extending the range
of the search.

00:29:51.452 --> 00:29:54.615
Tuvok, surely you must know
I'm here.

00:29:54.655 --> 00:29:57.556
We've shared so much.

00:29:59.627 --> 00:30:02.289
I'm just not getting anything.

00:30:02.329 --> 00:30:05.264
Nor am I.

00:30:05.299 --> 00:30:07.426
I felt empty...

00:30:07.468 --> 00:30:09.527
alone.

00:30:09.570 --> 00:30:10.628
Maybe you're right.

00:30:10.671 --> 00:30:11.968
What I sensed
wasn't the Captain.

00:30:12.006 --> 00:30:14.566
It was me wanting to believe
she wasn't dead.

00:30:14.608 --> 00:30:18.977
We've been trying
for three days without success,

00:30:19.079 --> 00:30:22.310
nor have Lieutenant Torres
and Ensign Kim found

00:30:22.349 --> 00:30:24.408
any indication
that the Captain is alive.

00:30:24.451 --> 00:30:27.818
There is a point
at which we must accept

00:30:27.855 --> 00:30:30.016
the inevitability of her death.

00:30:34.628 --> 00:30:36.755
Thank you for helping.

00:30:36.797 --> 00:30:39.994
I don't think I would have
accepted it if you hadn't

00:30:40.034 --> 00:30:41.592
at least tried.

00:30:41.635 --> 00:30:43.466
Good night.

00:30:54.715 --> 00:30:57.206
Tactical Officer's Log,
supplemental.

00:30:57.251 --> 00:31:00.812
My attempt to help Kes
detect the Captain's presence

00:31:00.854 --> 00:31:02.617
has ended in failure.

00:31:02.656 --> 00:31:06.217
I am forced to conclude
that we have, in fact,

00:31:06.260 --> 00:31:08.421
lost Kathryn Janeway.

00:31:08.462 --> 00:31:10.953
I would like the record to show

00:31:10.998 --> 00:31:14.832
that I have lost
a good friend as well,

00:31:14.868 --> 00:31:18.395
one whom I can never replace.

00:31:18.439 --> 00:31:20.407
Oh, Tuvok.

00:31:20.441 --> 00:31:21.965
They all love you, Kathryn.

00:31:22.076 --> 00:31:25.068
It's going to be hard for them.

00:31:25.112 --> 00:31:26.340
This can't be happening.

00:31:26.380 --> 00:31:27.404
I don't believe it.

00:31:27.448 --> 00:31:29.040
Because you don't want to.

00:31:30.451 --> 00:31:34.319
Tomorrow, it will become easier.

00:31:37.358 --> 00:31:39.383
My memorial service.

00:31:39.426 --> 00:31:43.726
When I came to this ship,
I resented the fact

00:31:43.764 --> 00:31:45.789
that Captain Janeway
was responsible

00:31:45.833 --> 00:31:48.893
for our being stranded here
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:31:51.505 --> 00:31:53.871
I didn't think that she made
the right decision

00:31:53.907 --> 00:31:59.368
and I certainly didn't want
to serve under her command.

00:31:59.413 --> 00:32:03.213
In the beginning,
I fought her.

00:32:04.852 --> 00:32:07.878
Even when she made me
Chief Engineer, I...

00:32:07.921 --> 00:32:10.185
I didn't trust her reasons.

00:32:10.224 --> 00:32:13.955
I kept looking
for a hidden agenda.

00:32:14.061 --> 00:32:18.122
I actually believed
that she'd set me up to fail.

00:32:18.165 --> 00:32:21.293
Well, I couldn't
have been more wrong.

00:32:21.335 --> 00:32:25.396
She saw...
she saw something in me

00:32:25.439 --> 00:32:27.100
that I didn't see.

00:32:27.141 --> 00:32:29.735
She saw a worthwhile person

00:32:29.777 --> 00:32:33.645
where I saw a lost
and hostile misfit,

00:32:33.680 --> 00:32:36.148
and because she had faith in me,

00:32:36.183 --> 00:32:39.209
I began to have faith in myself

00:32:39.253 --> 00:32:41.813
and when she died,
the first thing I thought

00:32:41.855 --> 00:32:43.618
was that I couldn't
do this without her,

00:32:43.657 --> 00:32:46.922
that I needed her too badly...

00:32:46.960 --> 00:32:51.897
her strength and her compassion,

00:32:51.932 --> 00:32:54.457
but then I realized

00:32:54.501 --> 00:32:58.597
that the gift that she gave me...
and gave a lot of us here...

00:32:58.639 --> 00:33:01.733
was the knowledge
that we are better

00:33:01.775 --> 00:33:04.005
and stronger than we think.

00:33:06.947 --> 00:33:09.279
I wish I had said
these things to her.

00:33:09.316 --> 00:33:12.649
I wish I had taken the time.

00:33:24.932 --> 00:33:26.695
Would anyone else
like to say something?

00:33:26.733 --> 00:33:27.757
I would, sir.

00:33:34.942 --> 00:33:37.433
I know Captain Janeway
wouldn't want us

00:33:37.478 --> 00:33:39.343
to be sitting around moping.

00:33:39.379 --> 00:33:42.473
She'd want us to be
cheering each other up,

00:33:42.516 --> 00:33:45.280
remembering the good times,
like the away mission

00:33:45.319 --> 00:33:49.187
when we found all those
bushes of overripe fruit.

00:33:49.223 --> 00:33:50.986
I must have eaten half a kilo.

00:33:51.058 --> 00:33:54.152
My hands and mouth
were all purple

00:33:54.194 --> 00:33:57.061
and the Captain...

00:34:02.503 --> 00:34:05.666
the Captain came
and sat down next to me,

00:34:05.706 --> 00:34:09.540
and her mouth
was all stained, too.

00:34:09.576 --> 00:34:12.875
She put her arm
around my shoulder...

00:34:16.683 --> 00:34:18.583
and she said...

00:34:23.757 --> 00:34:25.224
she said...

00:34:28.262 --> 00:34:29.957
"Ensign,

00:34:30.030 --> 00:34:32.931
these are the times
we have to remember."

00:34:35.235 --> 00:34:37.135
Lt...

00:34:39.573 --> 00:34:42.804
it's... Sorry.

00:34:51.218 --> 00:34:53.413
I know this hasn't been easy,

00:34:53.453 --> 00:34:55.978
but I think we'll all
be better for it.

00:34:56.023 --> 00:34:59.254
We will honor the Captain
one last time.

00:35:04.731 --> 00:35:07.427
Release the pod.

00:35:26.553 --> 00:35:28.214
Ensign Kim was right
when he said

00:35:28.255 --> 00:35:30.155
the Captain wouldn't
want us to be sad.

00:35:30.190 --> 00:35:32.590
Neelix has prepared some food

00:35:32.626 --> 00:35:35.322
and it would be nice
if we could all get together

00:35:35.362 --> 00:35:37.592
and share the good times
we had with Captain Janeway.

00:35:46.039 --> 00:35:49.065
It's over, Kathryn.

00:35:49.109 --> 00:35:51.407
There's nothing
left for you here.

00:35:51.445 --> 00:35:53.413
Come with me.

00:36:02.990 --> 00:36:04.924
What do I do to leave here?

00:36:05.025 --> 00:36:06.185
Just decide.

00:36:06.226 --> 00:36:09.753
The only thing that keeps you
is your refusal to leave.

00:36:09.796 --> 00:36:12.890
You may be right in everything
you've said to me,

00:36:12.933 --> 00:36:15.197
but I'm not ready to accept it.

00:36:15.235 --> 00:36:17.203
I'm not ready to go.

00:36:19.640 --> 00:36:21.699
My poor little bird.

00:36:21.742 --> 00:36:23.937
You always made it
hard for yourself.

00:36:24.044 --> 00:36:27.780
If there was a rocky path
and a smooth one, you chose

00:36:27.913 --> 00:36:29.437
the rocky one every time.

00:36:29.481 --> 00:36:33.679
If I stay,
maybe it'll be easier for them.

00:36:33.719 --> 00:36:35.346
Maybe I could be
comforting somehow.

00:36:35.387 --> 00:36:38.288
You're saying all the things
I told myself

00:36:38.323 --> 00:36:40.291
when I refused to leave you.

00:36:40.325 --> 00:36:43.192
I was hoping you wouldn't
have to go through that.

00:36:45.230 --> 00:36:48.290
It's a horrible existence,
Kathryn.

00:36:48.333 --> 00:36:51.530
As time wears on,
you begin to see

00:36:51.570 --> 00:36:56.735
how potent, how destructive
loneliness is.

00:36:56.775 --> 00:37:00.506
You'll see the people you love
going on with their lives,

00:37:00.546 --> 00:37:03.276
doing all the things
you used to share with them,

00:37:03.315 --> 00:37:05.340
but you won't be
a part of it anymore.

00:37:05.384 --> 00:37:08.717
You'll be forever
shut out of their existence.

00:37:08.754 --> 00:37:12.246
It becomes agonizing.

00:37:12.291 --> 00:37:14.816
I don't want that
to happen to you.

00:37:16.995 --> 00:37:19.395
Maybe that's what it'll take
for me to make this decision.

00:37:19.431 --> 00:37:22.127
I just know that
now I'm not ready.

00:37:22.167 --> 00:37:24.135
What can I do to convince you?

00:37:24.169 --> 00:37:25.136
Nothing.

00:37:25.170 --> 00:37:28.071
I can't... I won't...
abandon them.

00:37:28.106 --> 00:37:29.368
We're too much
a part of each other.

00:37:29.408 --> 00:37:30.375
Can't you see that?

00:37:30.409 --> 00:37:33.606
We've been through
so much together.

00:37:33.645 --> 00:37:36.170
I have to know what's
going to happen to them...

00:37:36.215 --> 00:37:40.379
to see Kes continue
to grow and learn...

00:37:40.419 --> 00:37:43.183
to know if Tom and B'Elanna
will ever stop

00:37:43.222 --> 00:37:46.521
sparring with each other
and develop a real friendship.

00:37:46.558 --> 00:37:49.322
You can only be
an observer of their lives,

00:37:49.361 --> 00:37:50.658
never a participant.

00:37:50.696 --> 00:37:52.163
I don't care.

00:37:52.197 --> 00:37:54.222
I'd rather be here in spirit
than not at all.

00:37:54.266 --> 00:37:56.166
A Captain doesn't abandon ship.

00:37:56.201 --> 00:37:58.169
Every hour you stay here,

00:37:58.203 --> 00:37:59.932
makes it that much
more difficult to leave.

00:37:59.972 --> 00:38:01.530
Why are you pushing me?

00:38:01.573 --> 00:38:03.040
I've made up my mind.

00:38:03.075 --> 00:38:04.906
I'm staying here.

00:38:04.977 --> 00:38:06.604
The cortical stimulator
is working.

00:38:06.645 --> 00:38:07.839
I'm getting a weak pulse.

00:38:07.880 --> 00:38:08.869
She's coming back.

00:38:08.914 --> 00:38:11.178
I'll use cordrazine
along with the stimulator.

00:38:11.216 --> 00:38:12.513
What was that?

00:38:12.551 --> 00:38:13.711
What happened?

00:38:13.752 --> 00:38:14.810
What do you mean?

00:38:14.853 --> 00:38:17.447
I saw Tuvok and Chakotay
and the Doctor.

00:38:17.489 --> 00:38:18.854
Here?

00:38:18.891 --> 00:38:20.085
No, it was different.

00:38:20.125 --> 00:38:21.251
As though...

00:38:21.293 --> 00:38:23.693
as though I were
looking up at them.

00:38:23.729 --> 00:38:25.594
An hallucination,
like the others.

00:38:25.631 --> 00:38:27.064
It didn't feel like the others.

00:38:27.099 --> 00:38:28.430
I didn't see myself.

00:38:28.467 --> 00:38:30.230
I was looking up at them.

00:38:32.838 --> 00:38:35.329
That's the real me, isn't it?

00:38:35.374 --> 00:38:38.366
Lying on the ground
on that planet dying.

00:38:40.178 --> 00:38:41.907
And this is the hallucination.

00:38:41.947 --> 00:38:43.175
This isn't real.

00:38:43.215 --> 00:38:44.182
More denial.

00:38:44.216 --> 00:38:46.411
You're only making it
harder on yourself.

00:38:46.451 --> 00:38:49.249
You're trying very hard
to convince me to come with you.

00:38:49.288 --> 00:38:50.277
Why is that?

00:38:50.322 --> 00:38:51.812
If what you're saying is true,

00:38:51.857 --> 00:38:54.325
why not let me come
to the decision on my own?

00:38:54.359 --> 00:38:57.385
I'm trying to spare you
unnecessary pain.

00:38:57.429 --> 00:39:00.364
My father
would never act like this.

00:39:00.399 --> 00:39:03.027
He always believed
I had to learn my own lessons,

00:39:03.068 --> 00:39:04.865
make my own mistakes.

00:39:04.903 --> 00:39:07.770
He never tried
to shield me from life.

00:39:07.806 --> 00:39:11.401
Why would he try
to shield me from death?

00:39:12.444 --> 00:39:14.469
You're not my father.

00:39:14.513 --> 00:39:17.676
I could be imagining you,
but I don't think so.

00:39:17.716 --> 00:39:20.480
You have such a specific agenda.

00:39:20.519 --> 00:39:23.750
You're determined
that I go with you somewhere.

00:39:23.789 --> 00:39:25.723
Who are you?

00:39:25.757 --> 00:39:27.725
I'm trying to help you.

00:39:27.759 --> 00:39:29.192
Stop fighting me.

00:39:29.227 --> 00:39:32.355
Are you an alien being
of some kind?

00:39:32.397 --> 00:39:34.695
Is that it?

00:39:34.800 --> 00:39:35.698
Her eyes are open.

00:39:35.734 --> 00:39:37.326
Vital signs are responding.

00:39:37.369 --> 00:39:38.893
Blood pressure is 60/30.

00:39:38.937 --> 00:39:40.268
But the entity
is still inhabiting

00:39:40.305 --> 00:39:41.272
her cerebral cortex,

00:39:41.306 --> 00:39:42.739
impeding your treatment.

00:39:42.774 --> 00:39:43.741
Kathryn, hang on.

00:39:43.775 --> 00:39:44.742
We're bringing you back.

00:39:44.776 --> 00:39:45.868
Just fight a little longer.

00:39:45.911 --> 00:39:47.310
Direct synaptic stimulation

00:39:47.346 --> 00:39:49.211
might drive out
the alien presence.

00:39:49.247 --> 00:39:51.647
I was right.

00:39:51.683 --> 00:39:54.174
I heard Tuvok and Chakotay
and the Doctor.

00:39:54.219 --> 00:39:56.050
You're an alien.

00:39:56.088 --> 00:39:58.921
You've created all these
hallucinations, haven't you?

00:39:58.957 --> 00:40:00.948
This is what my species does.

00:40:01.026 --> 00:40:02.891
At the moment just before death,

00:40:02.928 --> 00:40:05.726
one of us comes to help you
understand what's happening...

00:40:05.764 --> 00:40:08.358
to make the crossing over
an occasion of joy.

00:40:08.400 --> 00:40:09.799
And what is that?

00:40:10.836 --> 00:40:12.167
Our matrix...

00:40:12.204 --> 00:40:14.263
where your consciousness
will live.

00:40:14.306 --> 00:40:15.295
I was being truthful

00:40:15.340 --> 00:40:17.774
when I said it was
a place of wonder.

00:40:17.809 --> 00:40:20.437
It can be
whatever you want it to be.

00:40:20.479 --> 00:40:23.380
Then why didn't you tell me this
from the beginning?

00:40:23.415 --> 00:40:24.973
Why pretend to be my father?

00:40:25.083 --> 00:40:27.984
Usually people are comforted
to see their loved ones.

00:40:28.020 --> 00:40:30.989
It makes the crossing over
a much less fearful occasion.

00:40:31.056 --> 00:40:33.752
I've done this many times,

00:40:33.792 --> 00:40:37.922
but I've never encountered
someone so resistant.

00:40:37.963 --> 00:40:39.328
Something's happening.

00:40:39.364 --> 00:40:41.298
The alien presence is
getting stronger again.

00:40:41.333 --> 00:40:43.392
Fight it, Kathryn, fight it
just a little longer.

00:40:43.435 --> 00:40:45.960
I'll have to try a thoron pulse.

00:40:46.004 --> 00:40:48.097
My people are telling me
to fight.

00:40:48.140 --> 00:40:49.300
They're trying to save me.

00:40:49.341 --> 00:40:50.899
They're trying
out of desperation.

00:40:50.942 --> 00:40:51.909
It's hopeless.

00:40:51.943 --> 00:40:53.501
You're the one
who sounds desperate.

00:40:53.545 --> 00:40:54.512
I don't get the feeling

00:40:54.546 --> 00:40:55.808
you're trying to make
me comfortable.

00:40:55.847 --> 00:40:58.213
You're only interested
in my agreeing to come with you.

00:40:58.250 --> 00:40:59.979
Because it's inevitable.

00:41:00.018 --> 00:41:02.885
And you don't strike me
as any kind of good Samaritan.

00:41:02.921 --> 00:41:04.513
You're more like a vulture,

00:41:04.556 --> 00:41:06.683
preying on people at
the moment of their death

00:41:06.725 --> 00:41:08.090
when they're most vulnerable.

00:41:08.126 --> 00:41:10.094
I've waited for you.
I've been patient.

00:41:10.128 --> 00:41:12.221
But your patience
is wearing thin.

00:41:12.264 --> 00:41:14.596
What's the real reason you
want me in that matrix?

00:41:14.633 --> 00:41:16.726
Somehow I don't think
it has anything to do

00:41:16.768 --> 00:41:17.826
with everlasting joy.

00:41:19.438 --> 00:41:20.803
You must go with me.

00:41:20.839 --> 00:41:24.172
If you could force me to go,
you'd have done it already.

00:41:24.209 --> 00:41:26.074
You need me to agree,
don't you?

00:41:26.111 --> 00:41:27.772
I have to go voluntarily.

00:41:27.813 --> 00:41:28.802
Wouldn't that be better

00:41:28.847 --> 00:41:30.712
than standing here
in this endless debate?

00:41:30.749 --> 00:41:32.216
Let me tell you this.

00:41:32.250 --> 00:41:34.718
We can stand here
for all eternity

00:41:34.753 --> 00:41:37.779
and I will never
choose to go with you.

00:41:40.025 --> 00:41:41.993
You're in a dangerous
profession, Captain.

00:41:42.027 --> 00:41:43.221
You face death every day.

00:41:43.261 --> 00:41:44.728
There'll be another time,

00:41:44.763 --> 00:41:46.094
and I'll be waiting.

00:41:46.131 --> 00:41:48.998
Eventually,
you'll come into my matrix

00:41:49.034 --> 00:41:54.233
and you will nourish me
for a long, long time.

00:41:55.707 --> 00:41:59.336
Go back to hell, coward.

00:42:03.949 --> 00:42:04.916
Kathryn?

00:42:04.950 --> 00:42:06.850
I'm no longer detecting
the alien presence.

00:42:06.885 --> 00:42:08.443
Vital signs are responding.

00:42:08.487 --> 00:42:11.081
Blood pressure 110/65.

00:42:17.729 --> 00:42:18.957
Doctor...

00:42:19.064 --> 00:42:20.531
what happened?

00:42:20.565 --> 00:42:22.863
Perhaps you can explain,
Commander.

00:42:22.901 --> 00:42:24.300
You and I were caught
in a magnetic storm

00:42:24.336 --> 00:42:25.394
and crashed here.

00:42:25.437 --> 00:42:26.529
You were badly injured.

00:42:26.571 --> 00:42:28.732
The Doctor just arrived
on a shuttle with Tuvok

00:42:28.773 --> 00:42:29.865
and began treating you.

00:42:29.908 --> 00:42:31.102
As he was doing so,

00:42:31.143 --> 00:42:34.374
we detected an alien presence
within your cerebral cortex.

00:42:34.412 --> 00:42:37.108
It appeared to be preventing
our attempts to heal you.

00:42:37.149 --> 00:42:38.776
Eventually, it was dislodged,

00:42:38.817 --> 00:42:41.479
but there were a number of times
I thought we'd lost you.

00:42:41.520 --> 00:42:44.387
But each time, you seemed
to fight back.

00:42:44.422 --> 00:42:45.946
He kept telling me to let go,

00:42:45.991 --> 00:42:47.219
but I wouldn't.

00:42:47.259 --> 00:42:48.658
"He"?

00:42:48.693 --> 00:42:49.682
My fa...

00:42:51.730 --> 00:42:52.992
The alien.

00:42:53.064 --> 00:42:56.966
He wanted to take me
into another place.

00:42:57.002 --> 00:42:58.629
Another place?

00:42:58.670 --> 00:43:00.433
Some kind of afterlife?

00:43:02.874 --> 00:43:04.569
Maybe,

00:43:04.609 --> 00:43:06.941
but I can tell you this...

00:43:06.978 --> 00:43:09.208
from what I saw,

00:43:09.247 --> 00:43:13.149
it's certainly not where
I'd like to spend eternity.

00:43:27.299 --> 00:43:30.757
Captain's Log, Stardate 50518.6.

00:43:30.802 --> 00:43:32.599
The Doctor has examined me
thoroughly

00:43:32.637 --> 00:43:34.366
and pronounced me
physically fit,

00:43:34.406 --> 00:43:36.306
but I'll admit that it will
take a little longer

00:43:36.341 --> 00:43:39.833
to work through the emotional
impact of my experience.

00:43:41.112 --> 00:43:42.443
Come in.

00:43:43.648 --> 00:43:45.616
I could have sworn I
heard the Doctor tell you

00:43:45.650 --> 00:43:46.776
to take it easy
for a few days.

00:43:46.818 --> 00:43:49.412
Taking it easy usually
makes me feel worse.

00:43:49.454 --> 00:43:50.546
You shouldn't push yourself.

00:43:50.589 --> 00:43:51.647
You've been through a lot.

00:43:51.690 --> 00:43:53.180
Aw...

00:43:56.294 --> 00:43:57.989
To tell you the truth,

00:43:58.029 --> 00:44:01.487
I'd rather stay busy
than dwell on what happened.

00:44:01.533 --> 00:44:03.296
I can understand that.

00:44:03.335 --> 00:44:07.237
I can't help thinking about it...
that alien, his matrix.

00:44:07.272 --> 00:44:08.603
He was like the spider

00:44:08.640 --> 00:44:10.733
who has to lure a fly
into his web.

00:44:10.775 --> 00:44:12.936
Do you think it's possible

00:44:13.011 --> 00:44:15.104
that each
of the near-death experiences

00:44:15.146 --> 00:44:18.274
we've heard about are the result
of an alien inhabitation?

00:44:18.316 --> 00:44:20.511
That's a little hard to believe.

00:44:20.552 --> 00:44:23.248
I hope so.

00:44:23.288 --> 00:44:25.313
I'd prefer to think
his species was unique

00:44:25.357 --> 00:44:26.415
to the Delta Quadrant

00:44:26.458 --> 00:44:28.517
and that I've seen
the last of him.

00:44:28.560 --> 00:44:30.585
I'm sure that's the case.

00:44:30.629 --> 00:44:32.620
After going head-to-head
with Kathryn Janeway,

00:44:32.664 --> 00:44:34.928
he must have realized
he'd met his match.

00:44:34.966 --> 00:44:36.934
Come on, Chakotay.

00:44:39.471 --> 00:44:40.665
I cheated death.

00:44:40.705 --> 00:44:42.969
That's worth a celebration,
don't you think?

00:44:43.074 --> 00:44:44.336
A bottle of champagne...

00:44:44.376 --> 00:44:46.435
moonlight sail on Lake George.

00:44:46.478 --> 00:44:47.445
How does that sound?

00:44:47.479 --> 00:44:49.037
Like something worth living for.
